  "refinements": [
    "Actual allocation census separates ordinary native device storage from RC-backed TLS context/strings, shared string lists and RC code with managed data roots",
    "TLS server raw context reader and Scheme client-psettings retention are both actual users; one context plus up to five string fields is a source-shaped obligation count, not a runtime measurement",
    "Owner drain, same-address storage adoption and independent native allocation from birth have distinct authority/alias/deallocator admission conditions",
    "Pre-reserved handoff work owns the source-to-target commit and target-to-task publication gap; failure after membership commit cannot restore source rollback authority",
    "Migrated RC/list/ref/data entry points must serialize or exclude all legacy back doors; native bytes with managed data require a Gambit safe collector/root ownership cut",
    "Still-object head detachment leaves a real private discovery cursor; permitted derived births and all release origins retain source permits through known disposition or actual transfer",
    "Wrapper storage cannot be freed while a task borrows its fields; capacity/exception/unknown-alias cases retain actual dependent custody instead of dropping credit",
    "Prepare roots before VM scan synchronization destruction; replace registry-lock-held dependent waits with pinned identity and revalidated cleanup frontiers",
    "Operational wait ranks exclude admitted internal blocking cycles only under complete dependency census; same-lane children yield and owner-dependent callbacks remain in a live-owner phase",
    "Ten post-reuse support obligations, six maintenance events and five economic conditions credit modern C donor transfer/funnels/generation; positive Zig-only and total bounds remain unresolved"
  ],
